# FINAL COOLING-OFF EXIT COMPLETION -- IMPLEMENTATION AND MANUAL VERIFICATION
# The coding agent only read/edited files. Compilation, startup, HTTP requests,
# Kafka delivery, Oracle changes and end-to-end tests have NOT been executed.
# This file supersedes the earlier stage's "do not complete yet" descriptions.
#
# CREATED
# LoanAccount:
#   .env.example
#   config/InternalExitSecurityConfig.java
#   controller/InternalExitController.java
#   controller/InternalExitErrors.java
#   service/CoolingOffLoanClosureService.java
# Exit Service:
#   completion/LoanAccountClosureClient.java
#   completion/FinalExitStateService.java
#   completion/FinalExitCompletionService.java
#   completion/FinalExitRecovery.java
#   final-completion-manual.http
#   final-completion-verification.sql
# MODIFIED
# LoanAccount: pom.xml, src/main/resources/application.properties
# Exit Service: application.properties, .env.example, events/PaymentEventConsumer.java,
#   events/PaymentConfirmationService.java, events/LoanExitEventProducer.java
# Frontend: BorrowerDashboard.jsx, components/SettlementPayment.jsx
# Earlier stage guides/SQL: pointers to the current final-state requirements.
# No new microservice, DB table/column, user login, Kafka contract or gateway route.
# Razorpay credentials, borrower/officer signing and Collateral Service are unchanged.
#
# SERVICE OWNERSHIP
# Payment + Exit code live in clearclose-exit-service (8083).
# LoanAccount (backend/LoanAccount, 8085) owns the LOAN_ACCOUNT closure write.
# clearclose-loan-service (8090) remains the borrower loan read API; it is not used
# to write closures. The current services share Oracle, but remote/local updates
# are deliberately separate transactions, never treated as one distributed commit.
#
# FLOW
# 1. Existing PaymentSucceeded validates against verified PAYMENT, event identity,
#    exact amount/INR, all workflow relationships and recorded officer approval.
# 2. PaymentConfirmationService commits PAID + PAYMENT_EVENT_CONFIRMED first.
# 3. FinalExitCompletionService reads that durable work and calls LoanAccount
#    WITHOUT holding an Exit Service DB transaction or request/loan row locks.
# 4. LoanAccount independently verifies SUCCESS/provider/confirmation, PAID quote,
#    ACCEPTED_AT, officer/DECIDED_AT, amount, relationship IDs and confirmation audit.
#    In one local transaction it sets LOAN_STATUS=CLOSED, OUTSTANDING_AMOUNT=0,
#    CLOSURE_DATE=SYSDATE, UPDATED_AT=SYSTIMESTAMP and COOLING_OFF_LOAN_CLOSED audit.
# 5. Exit Service validates returned IDs/CLOSED/zero/date, and checks Oracle's exact
#    same-workflow closure marker. Only then does it change APPROVED -> COMPLETED,
#    preserving officer/decision fields and recording COOLING_OFF_EXIT_COMPLETED.
# 6. The existing producer persists a stable UUID/UTC time in LOAN_EXIT_EVENT_READY
#    in that same completion transaction, then sends LoanExitCompleted after commit.
#    The message key remains loanId. PaymentSucceeded continues to use quoteId.
# 7. Broker acknowledgement records LOAN_EXIT_EVENT_PUBLISHED in a NEW transaction.
#    Automatic retries reconstruct the original event identity from the audit log.
#
# INTERNAL API / AUTHENTICATION
# POST http://localhost:8085/api/internal/loans/{loanId}/complete-cooling-off-exit
# Body: {"paymentId": ..., "quoteId": ..., "exitRequestId": ...}
# It is NOT routed publicly by Gateway. Browser/user JWTs cannot authorize it.
# A separate service JWT uses HS256, issuer/sub clearclose-exit-service, audience
# clearclose-loan-account-internal, role EXIT_SERVICE, expiration 120 seconds.
# The dedicated high-priority security chain checks this identity only for the
# internal route. Normal LoanAccount borrower/officer security remains unchanged.
# A missing/placeholder service secret disables internal authentication, not security.
# Do not use the borrower JWT signing key as the service key. Never send it to Vite.
# Local direct HTTP is for this prototype; deployments must protect service traffic
# and use TLS/secret management. Tokens and service secrets are never logged here.
#
# REQUIRED SETUP (perform manually)
# Generate ONE random secret, at least 32 bytes, and set the SAME value in BOTH
# LoanAccount and Exit Service Java process/IDE environments:
#   EXIT_LOAN_SERVICE_SECRET=<your_random_secret>
# Other Exit Service settings:
#   LOAN_ACCOUNT_SERVICE_URL=http://localhost:8085
#   FINAL_EXIT_RETRY_DELAY_MS=30000
#   FINAL_EXIT_RETRY_BATCH_SIZE=20
# .env.example is a placeholder reference, not automatically loaded by Spring.
# In CMD you may generate a random 64-character value manually using:
#   powershell -NoProfile -Command "[guid]::NewGuid().ToString('N') + [guid]::NewGuid().ToString('N')"
# Copy it into the process environment with: set "EXIT_LOAN_SERVICE_SECRET=..."
# Do not paste actual secrets into tracked files or screenshots.
#
# STARTUP (separate CMD windows; adapt Java and repository paths if necessary)
# Kafka 4.3.1, already formatted -- do not format storage again:
#   cd /d C:\kafka_2.13-4.3.1
#   set "JAVA_HOME=C:\jdk25"
#   set "PATH=%JAVA_HOME%\bin;%PATH%"
#   set "KAFKA_HEAP_OPTS=-Xms512M -Xmx1G"
#   bin\windows\kafka-server-start.bat config\server.properties
# LoanAccount:
#   cd /d C:\MajorProject\Clear-Close\backend\LoanAccount
#   set "EXIT_LOAN_SERVICE_SECRET=<same_generated_value>"
#   mvnw.cmd compile
#   mvnw.cmd spring-boot:run
# Exit Service:
#   cd /d C:\MajorProject\Clear-Close\backend\clearclose-exit-service
#   set "JAVA_HOME=C:\jdk25"
#   set "PATH=%JAVA_HOME%\bin;%PATH%"
#   set "EXIT_LOAN_SERVICE_SECRET=<same_generated_value>"
#   set "KAFKA_BOOTSTRAP_SERVERS=localhost:9092"
#   mvnw.cmd compile
#   mvnw.cmd spring-boot:run
# LoanAccount targets Java 21; Java 25 can build/run it with the Maven release setting.
# Keep discovery, auth, API Gateway (8080), loan read service (8090) and frontend running.
# Rebuild/restart IDE instances instead if that is your usual workflow; do not start
# duplicate processes on ports 8083 or 8085. No extra completion server is needed.
#
# FRESH END-TO-END TEST
# Use a new genuine Test Mode loan/payment; do not rewrite old financial statuses.
# Borrower request -> officer APPROVED -> fresh quote accepted before its deadline
# -> Razorpay test payment -> backend verification SUCCESS -> PaymentSucceeded.
# Logs should show EXIT_COMPLETED and Published LoanExitCompleted with a stable ID.
# Execute final-completion-verification.sql for that payment ID.
# Expected: PAYMENT SUCCESS; quote PAID; loan CLOSED; outstanding 0; closure date set;
# request COMPLETED; assigned officer/DECIDED_AT preserved; one audit per transition.
# Borrower: click Refresh Exit Status (or request Refresh Status) to fetch actual
# request + quote + loans. The details show loan status, outstanding and closure date.
# Payment SUCCESS alone is not displayed as proof that final loan closure finished.
#
# KAFKA INSPECTION (from C:\kafka_2.13-4.3.1, separate CMD)
#   bin\windows\kafka-console-consumer.bat --bootstrap-server localhost:9092 --topic clearclose.payment.succeeded --from-beginning --property print.key=true
#   bin\windows\kafka-console-consumer.bat --bootstrap-server localhost:9092 --topic clearclose.loan-exit.completed --from-beginning --property print.key=true
#   bin\windows\kafka-console-consumer.bat --bootstrap-server localhost:9092 --topic clearclose.payment.succeeded.DLT --from-beginning --property print.headers=true
#   bin\windows\kafka-consumer-groups.bat --bootstrap-server localhost:9092 --describe --group clearclose-exit-payment-v1
#
# FAILURE TESTS / RECOVERY
# A: Stop LoanAccount, complete a new test payment. Payment stays SUCCESS, quote PAID,
#    request APPROVED, loan ACTIVE. Existing consumer retries then may use DLT.
#    The durable PAYMENT_EVENT_CONFIRMED audit remains pending work regardless of
#    offsets/DLT. Restore LoanAccount; the recovery worker retries automatically.
# B: Stop Exit Service after LoanAccount commits but before request completion.
#    The loan is CLOSED, request APPROVED, and matching closure audit persists.
#    Restart Exit Service; worker calls the same idempotent closure operation,
#    confirms its existing result and finishes the request without closing again.
# C: Replay the ORIGINAL valid PaymentSucceeded using kafka-verification.sql's
#    replay payload. Completed workflows skip the remote call and financial updates.
#    No duplicate closure/completion/READY audit and no new logical completion UUID.
# D: Stop Kafka after payment confirmation while LoanAccount is unavailable, then
#    restore LoanAccount. Recovery can complete the exit even with Kafka down;
#    LOAN_EXIT_EVENT_READY remains durable. Restart Kafka; the worker retries the
#    SAME completion UUID/time until publication is acknowledged and saved.
# E: FAILED/INITIATED/unverified payment, wrong amount, wrong workflow IDs, unaccepted
#    quote, missing officer decision, PENDING/REJECTED/CANCELLED request: no closure.
#    Use separate valid test cases/events; do not forge old successful records.
# F: Borrower/officer/missing JWT to internal endpoint: denied, no DB changes.
#    Mismatched service secret/audience/issuer or expired service JWT: denied.
# G: A loan already closed by another workflow: 409; no zeroing or successful exit.
# H: Repeated successful verify/refresh and duplicate Kafka delivery: existing result.
#
# DURABILITY / LIMITATIONS
# No new tables were needed: existing AUDIT_LOG transitions and request locks provide
# durable per-workflow identity. LoanAccount and Exit commit separately, so partial
# states are real and deliberately recoverable. Recovery scans every 30 seconds
# in bounded batches; it also resumes genuine previously confirmed PAID/APPROVED
# work on startup. It never manufactures a payment or bypasses officer approval.
# Permanent auth/config/data problems remain pending and logged until corrected.
# Monitor these logs and DLT; the scheduler does not make conflicts safe by retrying.
# Completion publication has a stable READY record until a PUBLISHED acknowledgement.
# Crash after Kafka accepts but before Oracle saves PUBLISHED can produce duplicate
# deliveries with the SAME eventId; downstream consumers must deduplicate. This is
# at-least-once delivery, not exactly-once financial processing or a distributed TX.
# Do not remove audit history required for deduplication/recovery.
# The earlier PaymentSucceeded commit-to-publish gap still has the existing manual
# replay strategy; it was not replaced with a new payment outbox in this task.
# No automatic collateral release, COLLATERAL writes, release requests or NOC.
# No old financial records were edited and no real payments were initiated by agent.

@loanAccount = http://localhost:8085
@gateway = http://localhost:8080
@borrowerToken = REPLACE_WITH_BORROWER_TOKEN
@loanId = 4199
@paymentId = 2
@quoteId = 2
@exitRequestId = 1

### Security negative test: a BORROWER token must NOT authorize closure (401/403)
POST {{loanAccount}}/api/internal/loans/{{loanId}}/complete-cooling-off-exit
Authorization: Bearer {{borrowerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"paymentId": {{paymentId}}, "quoteId": {{quoteId}}, "exitRequestId": {{exitRequestId}}}

### Security negative test: no token must NOT authorize closure (401)
POST {{loanAccount}}/api/internal/loans/{{loanId}}/complete-cooling-off-exit
Content-Type: application/json

{"paymentId": {{paymentId}}, "quoteId": {{quoteId}}, "exitRequestId": {{exitRequestId}}}

### Reuse current GET APIs to verify actual backend results
GET {{gateway}}/api/borrower/loans/{{loanId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{borrowerToken}}

### Actual completed request
GET {{gateway}}/api/cooling-off/requests/{{exitRequestId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{borrowerToken}}
